<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<LinearLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:app="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto"
    android:id="@+id/home_root"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="match_parent"
    android:background="@drawable/bg_home_gradient"
    android:orientation="vertical">

        <!-- No app bar: every tab draws its own 56dp header on the ground plane, so the shell has
             nothing to put in one. The AppBarLayout that used to sit here was inflated, given the
             status-bar inset and then set GONE on every single tab switch — a measure pass that
             rendered nothing. Edge-to-edge: the gradient (home_root) draws behind the status bar and
             each tab's content takes the top inset itself (setupEdgeToEdge). -->

        <!-- Content + overlaid bottom nav: the nav floats over the content so the
             server list scrolls UNDER a faint scrim rather than sitting on a solid bar. -->
        <FrameLayout
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="0dp"
            android:layout_weight="1">

            <FrameLayout
                android:id="@+id/main_content"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="match_parent">

            <!-- ==================== TAB HOST (fragment tabs) ==================== -->
            <!-- The shell's fragment container: one fragment per bottom-nav destination, kept alive
                 (hide/show, never replace) so scroll position and in-flight state survive a tab
                 switch. It hosts ALL THREE tabs — Главная (HomeFragment), Аккаунт (AccountFragment)
                 and Настройки (SettingsTabFragment); the shell itself holds only this container,
                 the scrim and the bottom bar.
                 Главная is attached at launch and the other two the first time their tab is
                 opened (see MainActivity.syncTabFragments). -->
            <androidx.fragment.app.FragmentContainerView
                android:id="@+id/tab_host"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:visibility="gone" />

            </FrameLayout>

            <!-- Faint gradient scrim (transparent -> surface): the content fades out
                 under the nav buttons so the bar reads as frameless, no solid fill.

                 80dp, halved from 160 on the owner's report from the device: «серый фон
                 от навигации нужно сделать меньше раза в 2 именно по размеру». At 160 it
                 covered roughly a fifth of a phone screen, so the fade read as a grey band
                 over the content rather than as the bar dissolving into it. The gradient
                 itself is what the owner wants — only its extent was ever wrong.

                 THIS 80 IS THE ZERO-INSET FIGURE AND NOTHING ELSE: 56dp of bar plus 24dp of
                 headroom above the icons. The bar below grows UPWARD by the window's bottom
                 inset (setupEdgeToEdge pads it so the icons clear the gesture pill), and a
                 scrim that stayed 80 tall while the icons climbed 24-48dp left them standing
                 above their own backdrop — the owner's second phone, the one with the gesture
                 bar. So setupEdgeToEdge adds the same inset to this height, reading the number
                 below as its baseline: the scrim is always bar + inset + headroom, and the
                 phone with no gesture bar keeps precisely the 80 it has today.
                 The DRAWABLE carries the fade at a constant 40dp so growing this height moves
                 the ramp up instead of stretching it; see bg_bottom_nav_scrim.xml. -->
            <View
                android:id="@+id/bottom_nav_scrim"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="80dp"
                android:layout_gravity="bottom"
                android:background="@drawable/bg_bottom_nav_scrim" />

            <!-- Custom bottom bar (replaces Material BottomNavigationView, which reserved tall
                 internal whitespace below the label and floated the items well above the edge).
                 A plain weighted row of icon+label hugs the very bottom, and the WHOLE system inset
                 is padded in at runtime (setupEdgeToEdge) so the buttons stand clear of the gesture
                 pill or the 3-button strip rather than sharing that strip with them. The bar is
                 wrap_content, so that padding grows it UPWARD: 56dp on a phone with no gesture bar,
                 and 56 + the inset on a phone with one. Anything drawn behind these buttons has to
                 follow that (see bottom_nav_scrim above) — that is the whole of the owner's «значки
                 выпали выше из-за слайдера внизу экрана»: the buttons moved, the backdrop did not.
                 (An earlier note here promised «a SMALL fixed bottom pad, a few dp» and the code
                 never did that; the full inset is the Material rule and the one that keeps a 48dp
                 touch target off the system strip.)
                 The destination set is Главная · Аккаунт · Настройки, in that order — three items.
                 Аккаунт used to require a LOGIN and deleted itself otherwise, which is the two-item
                 bar the owner photographed after pasting a подписка from the clipboard; it now
                 stands on a departament подписка as well, and signing in is something done INSIDE
                 it. There is no Серверы item: the owner removed that destination on 2026-07-26
                 (docs/design2026/11-app-structure.md 2.0) and none of its functions were moved
                 elsewhere.

                 THE BAR IS A FRAME AND NOT A ROW ANY MORE, and the reason is the indicator.
                 Handoff README §4: «Полоска активной вкладки ОДНА на всю панель и переезжает —
                 28x3dp, 280 мс ease-out-quart. Не три отдельные, которые гаснут и зажигаются.»
                 A pill that lives inside its own tab column can only ever fade out over here and
                 fade in over there; travelling needs one view whose x is free of the weighted row.
                 So the row of destinations and the single indicator are siblings in this frame,
                 and MainActivity.positionNavIndicator drives the indicator's translationX.

                 The id `bottom_nav` is unchanged and still names the whole bar — MainActivity
                 pads it with the system inset, shows/hides it, anchors snackbars to it and posts
                 to it, and every one of those is a plain View call that a FrameLayout answers
                 exactly as the LinearLayout did. -->
            <FrameLayout
                android:id="@+id/bottom_nav"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_gravity="bottom"
                android:background="@android:color/transparent"
                android:minHeight="56dp">

                <!-- The three destinations. Equal weights, and each column hugs the bottom edge
                     of the bar (§4: «вся группа прижата к нижнему краю, padding 6-9dp») rather
                     than floating in the middle of it. -->
                <LinearLayout
                    android:id="@+id/nav_items"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_gravity="bottom"
                    android:baselineAligned="false"
                    android:orientation="horizontal">

                    <LinearLayout
                        android:id="@+id/nav_home"
                        android:layout_width="0dp"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_weight="1"
                        android:background="@null"
                        android:clickable="true"
                        android:focusable="true"
                        android:gravity="center_horizontal|bottom"
                        android:orientation="vertical"
                        android:paddingTop="@dimen/space_6"
                        android:paddingBottom="9dp"
                        android:stateListAnimator="@anim/nav_press">

                        <!-- 26dp, and that is a DELIBERATE DEPARTURE from §4's 23.
                             23dp was ported correctly and the owner still read it as small on
                             the device: «иконки у кнопок навигацией слишком маленькие». The
                             prototype is a 360dp browser mock-up; a 412dp phone at 2.6x makes
                             the same number a smaller share of the bar than §4 was drawn
                             against. 26 is the largest that keeps the relationship the
                             original 23 was chosen for — the glyph still sits INSIDE the 28dp
                             indicator's width, so the mark never outgrows the bar under it —
                             and the label goes 11 -> 12sp with it (@style/BottomNavLabel) so
                             the stacked mark scales as one thing instead of growing a head.
                             Everything else in §4 holds: label flush under the glyph, group
                             hugged to the bottom edge, padding 6 / 9dp. -->
                        <ImageView
                            android:id="@+id/nav_home_icon"
                            android:layout_width="26dp"
                            android:layout_height="26dp"
                            android:importantForAccessibility="no"
                            app:srcCompat="@drawable/ic_nav_home"
                            app:tint="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant" />

                        <!-- Flush under the glyph (§4 «подпись вплотную, без зазора»): the
                             -1dp pulls the 14sp line box's own leading back out, so the label
                             sits on the icon rather than 3dp below it. -->
                        <TextView
                            android:id="@+id/nav_home_label"
                            android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                            android:layout_marginTop="-1dp"
                            android:text="@string/bottom_nav_home"
                            android:textAppearance="@style/BottomNavLabel"
                            android:textColor="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant" />

                    </LinearLayout>

                    <!-- 2nd item: the Account tab. It carried android:visibility="gone" and was
                         switched on only after a LOGIN; MainActivity.updateAccountNav now
                         shows it for a departament подписка too, so the user who pasted one
                         has somewhere to sign in. Starting visible costs nothing — the gate
                         runs in onResume, before the first frame — and it means the common
                         case is not a bar that grows an item under the user's eyes.
                         Still a weighted item: where the destination genuinely does not exist
                         (no backend in the build, no session and no departament подписка) it
                         goes GONE and the 2 remaining items take equal halves. The indicator
                         follows the columns' measured geometry, so it re-centres itself when
                         this one comes and goes — see MainActivity.positionNavIndicator. -->
                    <LinearLayout
                        android:id="@+id/nav_account"
                        android:layout_width="0dp"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_weight="1"
                        android:background="@null"
                        android:clickable="true"
                        android:focusable="true"
                        android:gravity="center_horizontal|bottom"
                        android:orientation="vertical"
                        android:paddingTop="@dimen/space_6"
                        android:paddingBottom="9dp"
                        android:stateListAnimator="@anim/nav_press">

                        <ImageView
                            android:id="@+id/nav_account_icon"
                            android:layout_width="26dp"
                            android:layout_height="26dp"
                            android:importantForAccessibility="no"
                            app:srcCompat="@drawable/ic_nav_account"
                            app:tint="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant" />

                        <TextView
                            android:id="@+id/nav_account_label"
                            android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                            android:layout_marginTop="-1dp"
                            android:text="@string/bottom_nav_account"
                            android:textAppearance="@style/BottomNavLabel"
                            android:textColor="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant" />

                    </LinearLayout>

                    <LinearLayout
                        android:id="@+id/nav_settings"
                        android:layout_width="0dp"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_weight="1"
                        android:background="@null"
                        android:clickable="true"
                        android:focusable="true"
                        android:gravity="center_horizontal|bottom"
                        android:orientation="vertical"
                        android:paddingTop="@dimen/space_6"
                        android:paddingBottom="9dp"
                        android:stateListAnimator="@anim/nav_press">

                        <ImageView
                            android:id="@+id/nav_settings_icon"
                            android:layout_width="26dp"
                            android:layout_height="26dp"
                            android:importantForAccessibility="no"
                            app:srcCompat="@drawable/ic_nav_settings"
                            app:tint="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant" />

                        <TextView
                            android:id="@+id/nav_settings_label"
                            android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                            android:layout_marginTop="-1dp"
                            android:text="@string/bottom_nav_settings"
                            android:textAppearance="@style/BottomNavLabel"
                            android:textColor="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant" />

                    </LinearLayout>

                </LinearLayout>

                <!-- THE ONE INDICATOR. 28x3dp, sitting 2dp off the bar's bottom edge, moved
                     to the selected column by translationX over @integer/motion_nav_indicator
                     (280ms) on ease_out_quart. It is a sibling of the destinations and never a
                     child of one, which is the whole difference between travelling and
                     blinking. Starts INVISIBLE: the first paint places it before showing it,
                     so it can never flash at x=0 on the way to Главная. -->
                <View
                    android:id="@+id/nav_indicator"
                    android:layout_width="28dp"
                    android:layout_height="3dp"
                    android:layout_gravity="bottom|start"
                    android:layout_marginBottom="@dimen/space_2"
                    android:background="@drawable/bg_nav_dot"
                    android:importantForAccessibility="no"
                    android:visibility="invisible" />

            </FrameLayout>

        </FrameLayout>

</LinearLayout>
